1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:23,160
Don't Lady Yugiri always look so beautiful?

2
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:24,520
Of course she does.

3
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:26,040
She's a legendary courtesan.

4
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:27,500
What makes her so legendary?

5
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:29,280
You're too young to understand.

6
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:37,840
Several months had passed since the legendary courtesan reluctantly left her old life.

7
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:46,340
However, Master Hebeah, the high-ranking government official who arranged her freedom, passed away due to sudden illness.

8
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:51,320
In accordance with his wishes, she was granted a portion of his fortune.

9
00:00:52,200 --> 00:01:01,680
Despite the security her inheritance lent her, she faced the unfortunate prospect of living out the rest of her life in a town where she knew no one, and no one knew her.

10
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:08,720
They don't call her a legend without good reason.

11
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:12,200
I bet that girl puts the folks over in Kamiyashi-shou to shame.

12
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:15,200
Why would she leave that lifestyle behind?

13
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:16,240
Fresh treats!

14
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:17,220
Come on by!

15
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:19,080
Shirako, Manju, and Dango!

16
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:21,240
Step right up and enjoy!

17
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:27,480
Listen up, everyone!

18
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,940
The time has come for us to take a stand!

19
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:31,960
We must bring back Saga right now!

20
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:32,860
Saga!

21
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:33,780
Saga!

22
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:34,740
Huh?

23
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:38,000
What a creep.

24
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:38,980
Let's go.

25
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:41,740
Attention!

26
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:44,880
Please stop by to watch our show!

27
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:49,240
It's the Shingoro Traveling Show!

28
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,340
We're only in town for seven days!

29
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:51,680
Saga!

30
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:52,320
Saga!

31
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:54,840
Here, please take one, sir!

32
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:55,700
Saga!

33
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:57,580
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

34
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:01,700
I'm sorry!

35
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:01,860
I'm sorry!

36
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:10,540
Watch where you're going!

37
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:12,100
I'm sorry!

38
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:12,940
I'm sorry!

39
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:21,220
I see you're outspreading propaganda again!

40
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:23,420
This time, you're coming with me!

41
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:24,960
Stop struggling!

42
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:31,260
Think I'll hold on to this for now.

43
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:38,400
Kiiichi Momazaki, why are you always out here causing me so much damned trouble?

44
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:41,640
Give it a rest before I haul you off to jail once and for all!

45
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:44,540
I just want the people to remember how Saga used to be!

46
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:45,320
Stop that thief!

47
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:46,240
He's getting away!

48
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:48,440
Don't move a muscle until I get back!

49
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:50,380
I'm coming!

50
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:54,860
Huh?

51
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:55,980
Oh.

52
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:58,240
Thank you, Ito.

53
00:02:58,940 --> 00:02:59,980
Yeah, sure.

54
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,980
You just never learn, do you?

55
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:08,960
During that time, the members of the Meiji government considered Saga to be a problematic prefecture.

56
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:17,620
And in the Bakumatsu period, it underwent westernization faster than other domains, making Saga a key location during the Reformation.

57
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:25,160
But, with uprisings by the former samurai class during Meiji 7 and the accompanying defeats, its glory was tarnished.

58
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:31,580
By Meiji 9, Saga had been divided up between two prefectures, Mizuma and Nagasaki.

59
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:35,300
This resulted in its total erasure from the map.

60
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:38,940
You need to stop getting into trouble.

61
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:43,500
One day you're going to get yourself in it bad, and I won't be there to help you.

62
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:45,080
I can't just stop.

63
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:46,620
I want Saga back.

64
00:03:47,020 --> 00:03:48,160
The way it used to be.

65
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:52,320
You're never going to accomplish anything if you keep doing this by yourself.

66
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:55,040
The Imperial Court still has their issues with Saga.

67
00:03:55,040 --> 00:04:00,300
On top of that, nobody wants a repeat of the Saga war.

68
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,720
But I'm not trying to start a war!

69
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:04,660
That's how it comes across.

70
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:07,500
Let's say the Saga does get its name back.

71
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:09,160
What happens after?

72
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,200
I hadn't thought of...

73
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:13,480
Alright, enough of that.

74
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:16,100
Set aside the restoration of Saga, okay?

75
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:18,160
Let's go check out the cherry blossoms.

76
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:19,540
You'll love it.

77
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:23,220
It'll make you forget all about that old Saga you're so fond of.

78
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:23,620
Promise!

79
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:24,240
Huh?

80
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:27,480
You know I'm not really interested in that kind of stuff.

81
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:30,960
Hey, where's the meat?

82
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:32,740
I ate it all.

83
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:34,700
I'm going to get you!

84
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:37,920
If you think you can take me on, you just try me!

85
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:42,360
Teacher, you know, you would be the talk of the town if you weren't always cooped up in here.

86
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:46,280
Plus, the cherry blossoms are in bloom, and I know where all the best viewing spots are.

87
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:51,500
You're free now.

88
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:54,020
You should explore the outside world.

89
00:04:54,020 --> 00:05:00,800
Wow, look at the battle!

90
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:04,740
Wow, look at the battle!

91
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:04,920
It's pretty!

92
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:05,100
It's pretty!

93
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:05,680
Huh?

94
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:09,200
Hmm?

95
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:09,940
Hmm.

96
00:05:09,940 --> 00:05:10,060
Hmm.

97
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:27,360
Hmm.

98
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:27,880
Hmm.

99
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:28,420
Hmm.

100
00:05:28,420 --> 00:05:52,620
Oh, is this yours?

101
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:56,420
Here.

102
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:58,920
Thank you, it is.

103
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:04,920
I bought it moments before.

104
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:05,920
Coming through!

105
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:07,920
Get out of the way!

106
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:09,920
Look out!

107
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:25,920
Please allow me to help you.

108
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:34,920
Oh no, I'm…

109
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:36,920
Here, use this.

110
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,920
Thank you very much.

111
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:42,920
Hey, this is mine.

112
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:47,420
I'm sorry, I had no idea.

113
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:53,420
I apologize for treating it like tissue paper.

114
00:06:53,420 --> 00:07:05,920
You'll feel better once you change it to some dry clothes.

115
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:08,420
Oh, what happened to you?

116
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:10,420
She's an angel.

117
00:07:10,420 --> 00:07:12,420
Huh?

118
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:14,420
I think I know who she is.

119
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:18,920
If I'm right, she's the legendary courtesan who moved to Saga at the end of last year.

120
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:19,920
Legendary?

121
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:20,920
Come on.

122
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,920
You mean you haven't heard of her?

123
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,920
Pay more attention to town gossip.

124
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:29,420
She's a renowned courtesan named Yugiri.

125
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:33,420
Her performances were unlike anything anyone in Edo had ever seen.

126
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:34,920
Men and women alike revered her.

127
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:39,920
Yugiri was in high demand to the point that her prices skyrocketed to an obscene amount.

128
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:41,920
No one could afford her entertainment anymore.

129
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:45,420
Leaders of the Restoration fought over her.

130
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:48,420
And it's rumored that the Meiji court almost fell apart because of it.

131
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:51,420
And now she lives in Saga?

132
00:07:51,420 --> 00:07:53,420
Don't fall in love.

133
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:55,420
I'm not in love!

134
00:07:55,420 --> 00:07:58,420
You couldn't possibly handle a woman like that.

135
00:07:58,420 --> 00:08:00,420
She's from a different world.

136
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:06,420
Maybe I could learn more about her world.

137
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:31,920
Maybe I could learn more about her world.

138
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:43,380
Hello again.

139
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:55,300
You didn't need to go through such trouble just for me.

140
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:59,100
I know it's not much, but I wanted to say thank you for, uh...

141
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:01,020
I am touched that you thought of me, though.

142
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:05,240
Thank you, but you should run along home now.

143
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:08,240
The people in town might get the wrong idea.

144
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:16,920
But I don't care what they think.

145
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:21,240
See, all this talk about you being from a different world,

146
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:24,880
the complicated details about your history don't matter to me.

147
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:28,200
In our saga, it'll be…

148
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:35,240
Pardon me. Does a man by the name of Kiichi Momazaki live here?

149
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:39,460
Uh…

150
00:09:39,460 --> 00:09:55,460
Pardon me. Does a man by the name of Kiichi Momazaki live here?

151
00:09:55,460 --> 00:10:13,680
It's Saga. I am Saga. No, Saga is me!

152
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:20,900
Oh my! Are you all right, my lord?

153
00:10:20,900 --> 00:10:24,900
Grandpa, did you wander off?

154
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:30,120
This is a remedy for colds and other illnesses.

155
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:32,120
A very nourishing collection of herbs.

156
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:35,120
I asked an old acquaintance to send it to me.

157
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:37,120
That's so kind of you. Thank you.

158
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:39,120
I was feeling a little guilty.

159
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:43,340
You braved that blazing sun just to bring me a simple gift of gratitude.

160
00:10:43,340 --> 00:10:47,340
It's nothing. Besides, I wanted to do it.

161
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:49,340
It was so thoughtful.

162
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:53,340
Since I arrived in Saga, you're the first one to come calling,

163
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:55,340
other than my dance students.

164
00:10:55,340 --> 00:10:59,840
I must apologize for my grandpa earlier.

165
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:02,340
He's a little unwell.

166
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:06,220
He seemed like an interesting man to me.

167
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:08,880
He was already on the decline.

168
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:12,800
But I think when Saga lost its name, he got even worse.

169
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:16,860
He started ranting some nonsense about how he'd be able to raise the dead

170
00:11:16,860 --> 00:11:20,740
if only he had his old powers back.

171
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:25,980
About eight years ago, a big battle took place right here in Saga,

172
00:11:25,980 --> 00:11:29,320
and my father was killed.

173
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:32,280
After that, I had no place to go.

174
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:35,580
I spent my days cowering in the wilderness.

175
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:40,300
I don't know what would have happened if Gramps hadn't found me.

176
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:43,340
I owe him more than I could ever give him.

177
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:45,380
The only thing he cares about,

178
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:48,080
the only thing he wants in return,

179
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:50,340
is for me to save Saga.

180
00:11:50,340 --> 00:11:53,380
At first, I was confused by what that meant.

181
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:56,220
But then, when Saga lost its name,

182
00:11:56,220 --> 00:12:00,480
it felt like everything my father died trying to protect slipped away.

183
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:03,680
And Saga might vanish from people's hearts, too.

184
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:06,400
But I couldn't let that happen.

185
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:10,480
I think that fate is responsible for bringing my grandpa and I together,

186
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:13,240
so that I could find my purpose in life.

187
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:19,220
Yugiri, from this day forward,

188
00:12:19,220 --> 00:12:22,260
this is where you'll be living.

189
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:28,020
Finally, I have a clear vision for the future.

190
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:31,200
I know in my heart what I want to do now.

191
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:33,860
I want to create a new Saga.

192
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:38,740
A place where it doesn't matter what your status is or who you were before.

193
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:41,960
A place where anyone can choose their own paths in life,

194
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:44,580
and they can stay true to themselves.

195
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:45,620
Mm.

196
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:46,840
I see.

197
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:49,800
That sounds like a beautiful place to live.

198
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:55,460
Take one!

199
00:12:55,460 --> 00:12:57,140
Please take one, sir!

200
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:58,420
You there!

201
00:12:58,420 --> 00:13:00,100
You want to get arrested?

202
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:03,220
Very funny!

203
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:05,220
You never give up, do you?

204
00:13:09,220 --> 00:13:11,720
Um, Yugiri helped me out some.

205
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:13,720
Fixing the composition and stuff.

206
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:18,320
Oh, haha, there, there.

207
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:20,320
There, it's okay.

208
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,620
Don't cry.

209
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:40,220
I'm here with our dinner.

210
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:42,220
I'm here with our dinner.

211
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:46,240
Do forgive me, sir.

212
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:49,740
I felt an eerie presence, and perhaps I'm a little unnerved.

213
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:51,740
I'm so sorry!

214
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:53,580
I know I'm running late.

215
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:54,480
Huh?

216
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:57,240
Yito, you came early.

217
00:13:57,240 --> 00:14:01,000
I guess I couldn't wait to meet the legendary courtesan, Yugiri.

218
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,540
Look, this big one is for you.

219
00:14:03,540 --> 00:14:05,100
So huge!

220
00:14:05,100 --> 00:14:07,640
You actually caught that thing in the Fukushoe River?

221
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:08,600
Wow!

222
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:27,900
Tasty!

223
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:31,440
I see your exceptional skills extend to cooking, as well.

224
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:36,320
The man who arranged my freedom for me taught me all kinds of new talents.

225
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:39,240
They've helped me to live in the outside world since.

226
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:41,240
Hmm.

227
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,240
I bet he did.

228
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:47,460
Perhaps you should do the same.

229
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:48,460
Same what?

230
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:52,140
I mean, it's never a bad idea to learn new skills.

231
00:14:52,140 --> 00:14:54,300
You could become a scholar or a doctor.

232
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:58,180
If you really want to help people, you should focus on realistic goals,

233
00:14:58,180 --> 00:15:01,820
instead of wasting your time trying to bring back the glory days of Saga.

234
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:12,200
You happened upon this nice lady.

235
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,820
Maybe it was a sign.

236
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:14,820
You know?

237
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:17,060
Maybe it's time for you to start a family.

238
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:18,060
Huh?

239
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:21,600
Being the head of a household gives a man a feeling of responsibility.

240
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:23,060
Don't you want that?

241
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:24,600
the game?

242
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:25,600
Huh?

243
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:29,600
No way!

244
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:30,760
Are you stupid!?

245
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:32,300
Seriously, what are you saying?

246
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:34,440
Why on earth made you say something so crazy?

247
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:41,320
Oh my.

248
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:44,980
Are you alright?

249
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:46,980
Right? Lord Kiichi?

250
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:50,580
He's always been such a lightweight.

251
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:56,020
That's all right.

252
00:15:59,940 --> 00:16:01,220
Have one with me.

253
00:16:01,220 --> 00:16:03,140
No, I'm fine.

254
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:11,940
Tell me, Lord Ito,

255
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:15,300
just how long have you and Lord Kiichi known each other?

256
00:16:15,300 --> 00:16:17,780
We only met two years ago.

257
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:22,260
I heard about some oddball who was passing out strange pamphlets in the streets.

258
00:16:22,260 --> 00:16:24,580
I was amused at first.

259
00:16:24,580 --> 00:16:26,580
People seemed to ignore him,

260
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:29,620
walking right past him as if he weren't there.

261
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:31,220
Yet he never gave up.

262
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:33,380
He was so determined.

263
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:36,500
There had to be better ways to get the word out, but

264
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:38,900
to be honest, he's a fool.

265
00:16:42,820 --> 00:16:46,500
This country's changed, and it's going to keep changing fast.

266
00:16:47,540 --> 00:16:50,340
Nothing good will ever come of clinging to history.

267
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:54,420
I don't think Kiichi has any interest in bringing back the past.

268
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:57,700
He wants to create a more progressive saga.

269
00:17:00,260 --> 00:17:02,820
It might be nothing more than a fantasy right now,

270
00:17:02,820 --> 00:17:08,420
but he wants it, and I think that I want it too, to live in that saga.

271
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:21,380
Sooner or later, reality will set in, and he's going to get his heart broken.

272
00:17:22,260 --> 00:17:24,260
This country isn't ready for that saga.

273
00:17:25,300 --> 00:17:25,780
Not yet.

274
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:29,380
Thank you for this.

275
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:38,260
It was enlightening.

276
00:17:42,980 --> 00:17:44,260
Please take one!

277
00:17:44,260 --> 00:17:46,260
For Saga!

278
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:56,180
Sir, could you tell us more about the information in this handout?

279
00:17:56,180 --> 00:17:58,420
We're after the same things that you are.

280
00:17:58,420 --> 00:18:00,260
The old saga.

281
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:11,540
Those videos are there for the fact that you have this to match!

282
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:15,620
So, are there sleeping things?

283
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:19,380
Can you follow me unless I come out so,

284
00:18:21,220 --> 00:18:24,260
what can be shared in front of my ear?

285
00:18:24,260 --> 00:18:24,940
A default to her.

286
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:25,780
Nothing.

287
00:18:25,780 --> 00:18:26,580
I'm thankful for this.

288
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:56,560
Thank you.

